      "title": "3. A compact description of unequal circumstances",
      "text": "**Original:** “A consultative process should therefore include farmers whose land, income or household duties make participation difficult.”\n\n**Plain English:** Consultation should include farmers who find it hard to participate because of their circumstances.\n\n**Structure:** Subject + modal + verb + object extended by a possessive relative clause.\n\n**Main clause:** “A consultative process should therefore include farmers.”\n\n**Dependent clause:** “whose land, income or household duties make participation difficult” identifies relevant farmers and explains their barriers.\n\n**Important grammar:** *Whose* links the farmers to their circumstances. In “make participation difficult,” *participation* is the object and *difficult* is its complement: **make + object + adjective**. *Should* expresses a recommendation.\n\n**Vocabulary / collocation:** consultative process; household duties; make participation difficult.\n\n**Academic effect:** The sentence turns a broad principle of inclusion into specific conditions that policy must address.\n\n**New example:** “Universities should support applicants whose working hours make attendance difficult.”",
